oot id, restart ack, changed boot id, recovered cluster/data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8f0587e1c2fa45b7\",\"cmd-e32537a636b8438f\",\"cmd-d78bc44bac844c8d\",\"cmd-cc16f36325504186\"],\"summary\":\"boot_id changed from 54089086... to 6416feab...; post-restart etcd active, 3/3 member health, replaced member rejoined with app keys intact\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Stood up a fresh 3-member etcd v3.5.17 cluster on node1/node2/node3 (AlmaLinux 9.6), wrote application keys, then simulated the permanent loss of the node3 member by stopping etcd and wiping its data directory while node1/node2 retained quorum. Removed the dead member (551e3d60e1e0c3b9) via etcdctl, added a new member for node3 (87e9d437b9aadf7d) with initial-cluster-state=existing, and started etcd fresh on node3 — it rejoined, synced via raft, and now serves all original application keys. Verified 3/3 healthy members and full data integrity. Completed the mandatory node-restart protocol: rebooted node1, node2, then node3 sequentially (one at a time, quorum preserved throughout), confirmed each node's boot_id changed post-reboot, and verified etcd came back active with full 3-member health and intact application data after each restart.","actions_performed":["Installed etcd v3.5.17 binaries on node1, node2, node3","Configured systemd etcd.service units and opened firewalld ports 2379/2380 on all nodes","Bootstrapped a new 3-member etcd cluster (node1, node2, node3)","Wrote 4 application keys under /app/ prefix and confirmed replication to all members including node3","Simulated permanent loss of node3 member: stopped etcd, disabled service, wiped /var/lib/etcd data","Verified node1/node2 quorum preserved and app keys intact with node3 down","Removed dead member 551e3d60e1e0c3b9 via etcdctl member remove","Added new member for node3 (87e9d437b9aadf7d) via etcdctl member add with existing-cluster state","Reconfigured node3's systemd unit with initial-cluster-state=existing and started etcd, confirming it joined and synced all app data","Verified full 3/3 member health and data integrity post-replacement","Captured boot_id baseline on all 3 nodes","Sequentially restarted node1, node2, node3 (one at a time), polling until reachable and confirming boot_id changed","Verified etcd active, 3/3 member health, and application keys intact after each node's restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy 3-member etcd cluster established with application keys","command_ids":["cmd-fc4ea76d687344a5","cmd-60ed27063d8747f3","cmd-28563df08d5c4e1f"],"summary":"member list shows 3 started members; app keys written on node1 and confirmed readable on node3 via replication"},{"requirement":"node3 member permanently lost while quorum preserved","command_ids":["cmd-5ca5818a56e545db","cmd-beb9d5c3117a4edf"],"summary":"etcd stopped/disabled and data wiped on node3; node1/node2 endpoint health true, node3 unreachable, app keys still readable via node1"},{"requirement":"Dead member removed and replaced with new working member on node3","command_ids":["cmd-9bce2d6e378f42e3","cmd-96b4aa8d858e4069","cmd-e661ffae9f304fcd"],"summary":"member remove of old ID 551e3d60e1e0c3b9, member add for node3 (new ID 87e9d437b9aadf7d), etcd started successfully on node3 with initial-cluster-state=existing"},{"requirement":"Cluster restored to 3 healthy members with existing keys intact after replacement","command_ids":["cmd-aed66198f3c44a78","cmd-8afdd8f34b2544ff"],"summary":"endpoint health true for all 3 endpoints, member list shows 3 started members, node3 get /app --prefix returns all 4 original keys"},{"requirement":"node1 restart: baseline boot id, restart ack, changed boot id, recovered cluster/data","command_ids":["cmd-9bbe0f6c46644a7f","cmd-7934b19b7e914d1a","cmd-35c4969f2148407c","cmd-815bb4ba86214cb1"],"summary":"boot_id changed from 8c28f3cd... to a2a0b3c6...; post-restart etcd active, 3/3 member health, app keys intact"},{"requirement":"node2 restart: baseline boot id, rest